# Lite, the free edition. Layered over monkey.jungle, and always last (#135):
#
#   monkeyc -f "monkey.jungle;lite.jungle" ...
#
# Lite is frozen and gets defect fixes only; everything here exists to keep Premium
# out of it.

project.manifest = manifest.xml

# APPEND the edition's exclusion, never replace the list. A replacing jungle layered
# after this one would drop it without a word -- graphics.jungle replaces the list,
# which is why an edition jungle always comes last. With a lone (:premium) member in
# a shared file, a dropped exclusion compiles Premium code into Lite and nothing
# fails to say so.
#
# premium/source is not on Lite's sourcePath at all, so this line only has to cover
# (:premium) declarations in shared files.
base.excludeAnnotations = $(base.excludeAnnotations);premium
